{
 "_comment": "How each schema in RWA Sonar's attestation-types.json and finding-types.json would be said in Tokenizario's vocabulary v3 (rwa/data/tokenizario-vocabulary.json). This is the bridge that restates every attestation and finding instance in the database as 'X says Y about Z' without retyping it: rwa/lib/restatement.js applies it. fit: exact = a v3 type says it; approximate = a v3 type carries it only in its hashed text, so a recipe cannot test it; chain-fact = the reader reads it from the chain and nobody signs it; reading = the reader derives it from other statements; absence = it means a statement is missing, which a recipe shows as Missing; terms = it stays in the committed terms document by design; gap = v3 cannot say it (see gaps); out-of-scope = market data that is neither. signer is a role: issuer, custodian, auditor, transfer-agent, registrar, regulator, counsel, administrator, oracle, inspector, researcher (RWA Sonar itself, for findings), anyone.",
 "asOf": "2026-10-13",
 "vocabulary": "v3",
 "fits": [
